<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ production GDP falls s/adj 0.5 pct in March qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ production GDP falls s/adj 0.5 pct in March qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Monday released the following estimates of New Zealand's real, production-based gross domestic product for the quarter ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Economists estimated GDP would fall a seasonally adjusted 0.09 percent for the quarter for an annual rise of 1.95 percent.</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of New Zealand in its Monetary Policy Statement on Friday forecast GDP would rise a seasonally adjusted 0.3 percent for the quarter.</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter seasonally-adjusted figures (revised-from figures in brackets):</p>
<p>    March 1997		 Dec 1996		  March 1996</p>
<p>    -0.5 pct		   0.7 pct		   1.0 pct</p>
<p>S/adj change at constant prices from yr-ago quarter</p>
<p>    March 1997		 Dec 1996		  March 1996</p>
<p>    1.4 pct		    3.0 pct (2.9)	   2.8 pct</p>
<p>Real annual average change</p>
<p>    March 1997		 Dec 1996		  March 1996</p>
<p>    2.3 pct		    2.7 pct		   3.1 pct</p>
<p>Industries - quarterly pct change:</p>
<p>				   March 1997	 Dec 1996</p>
<p>    Agriculture		    0.6		 1.9</p>
<p>    Fishing, forestry, mining  6.6		-7.7</p>
<p>    Manufacturing		 -1.1		 1.4</p>
<p>    Power, gas, water	   -1.2		 5.8</p>
<p>    Construction		   3.0		 1.5</p>
<p>    Restaurants, hotels	  0.2		-1.2</p>
<p>    Dwellings			0.4		 0.4</p>
<p>    Transport, Communications -2.0		 2.4</p>
<p>    Govt services		 -1.2		 0.7</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
